      "writtenOn": "2024-11-20T19:16:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems right to me.\n\n`Send` looks OK because: The only `ABinderRpc_AccessorProvider` field is `std::weak_ptr\u003candroid::AccessorProvider\u003e`. `weak_ptr` is thread safe as long as the pointer itself isn\u0027t mutated, which seems to be true in this case. `android::AccessorProvider` looks safe because its fields are read only and the `std::function` field is calling into a rust function that we require to be `Send + Sync` via the `AccessorProvider::new` signature in rust.\n\n`Sync` looks OK in a trivial way because, there is nothing that can actually be done with an `AccessProvider` (i.e. there are no methods) besides dropping it.",
      "parentUuid": "0ca50bae_edf48be2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 262,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "f052bfbf930d125831b670c3287e672421fd308a",
